- name: xoshiro256
  type: table
  desc: Functions for interacting with the Xoshiro256 native extension
  members:
  - name: seed
    type: function
    desc: "Create state for the pseudo-random generator: equal seeds produce equal sequences of numbers. Accepts a number or a string (decimal representation of uint64, max 20 digits in the string) if full 64-bit precision required. State is seeded using splitmix64 algorithm."
    parameters:
    - name: seed
      type: number|string
    returns:
    - name: state
      type: userdata
  - name: random
    type: function
    desc: When called without arguments, returns a uniform pseudo-random real number in the range [0,1). When called with an integer number m, returns a uniform pseudo-random integer in the range [1, m]. When called with two integer numbers m and n, returns a uniform pseudo-random integer in the range [m, n].
    parameters:
    - name: state
      type: userdata
    - name: m
      optional: true
      type: number
    - name: n
      optional: true
      type: number
    returns:
    - name: value
      type: number
  - name: float_range
    type: function
    desc: Generates a random number in floating range [m, n)
    parameters:
    - name: state
      type: userdata
    - name: m
      type: number
    - name: n
      type: number
    returns:
    - name: value
      type: number
  - name: clone
    type: function
    desc: Creates and returns an independent copy of the state
    parameters:
    - name: state
      type: userdata
    - name: out
      optional: true
      type: userdata
    returns:
    - name: cloned_state
      type: userdata
  - name: to_string
    type: function
    desc: Convert state to string. Used for saving the state. String is formed as 4 uint64 values separated by ':', e.g. "s0:s1:s2:s3".
    parameters:
    - name: state
      type: userdata
    returns:
    - name: serialized_state
      type: string
  - name: from_string
    type: function
    desc: Convert previously saved string back to state.
    parameters:
    - name: serialized_state
      type: string
    returns:
    - name: state
      type: userdata
